  "text": "䃎Assistant\n\n}\";\n\nAssistant: To determine the least positive value of \\( t \\) such that the sequence\n\\[\n\\arccos(\\cos \\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos 3\\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos 11\\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos t\\alpha)\n\\]\nis an arithmetic progression for some \\( \\alpha \\) with \\( 0 < \\alpha < \\pi \\), we proceed step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Sequence\nAn arithmetic progression \\( a, b, c, d \\) satisfies:\n\\[\nb - a = c - b = d - c\n\\]\nThis implies:\n\\[\nb = a + d,\n\\]\nbut in this case, it holds true regardless of \\( d \\) as long as the differences are equal.\n\n### Step 2: Express the Sequence in Terms of \\( \\alpha \\)\nThe sequence becomes:\n\\[\n\\arccos(\\cos \\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos 3\\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos 11\\alpha), \\ \\arccos(\\cos t\\alpha)\n\\]\nFor the sequence to be arithmetic, the differences between consecutive terms must be equal:\n\\[\n\\cos 3\\alpha - \\cos \\alpha = \\cos 11\\alpha - \\cos 3\\alpha = \\cos t\\alpha - \\cos 11\\alpha\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Find Relationships Between \\( \\alpha \\) and \\( t \\)\nFrom \\( \\cos \\alpha + \\cos 3\\alpha = \\cos 11\\alpha - \\cos t\\alpha \\), we can derive:\n\\[\n\\cos \\alpha + \\cos 3\\alpha + \\cos t\\alpha = \\cos 11\\alpha\n\\]\nThis implies:\n\\[\n\\cos \\alpha + \\cos 3\\alpha + \\cos t\\alpha = \\cos 11\\alpha\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Simplify Using Trigonometric Identities\nUsing the identity \\( \\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A+B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A-B}{2}\\right) \\):\n\\[\n\\cos \\alpha + \\cos 3\\alpha = 2 \\cos 2\\alpha \\cos \\alpha\n\\]\nThus:\n\\[\n2 \\cos 2\\alpha \\cos \\alpha + \\cos t\\alpha = \\cos 11\\alpha\n\\]\nRearranging:\n\\[\n\\cos t\\alpha = \\cos 11\\alpha - 2 \\cos 2\\alpha \\cos \\alpha\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Solve for \\( t \\)\nFor the equation to hold, the right-hand side must be consistent with the left-hand side for some \\( \\alpha \\). Testing small values of \\( t \\), we find that:\n\\[\nt = 22\n\\]\nsatisfies the equation for \\( \\alpha = \\frac{\\pi}{30} \\).\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{22}\n\\]",
